# THE RED CONTROL of `same-bytes-alone` for what a worker hands on from unit to unit. The program of a-worker-that-has-walked-other-units-emits-what-a-fresh-one-emits.ir under
# testing=DisableLaterUnitSpeculation: `KeptBetweenUnits` remembers that the worker has begun a unit, and every later walk of that worker opens no guess: right code of another form, by what the worker did before.
# The fresh worker opens the guesses, and the run fails.
# OPTIONS: testing=DisableLaterUnitSpeculation threads=1
# PROGRAM-OF: a-worker-that-has-walked-other-units-emits-what-a-fresh-one-emits.ir
# DIAGNOSTIC: UnitCompiledAloneDiffers
# RUN: same-bytes-alone mechanisms=all
# CHECK: f4:Body differs:
# CHECK: f4:Body differs with every body in its place too
